## Problem

8 of 12 commands repeat a ~10-line dir-resolution dance (findTicketsDir,
optional override from args, os.Stat, IsDir check, error print). Three
commands (close, log, archive) also duplicate a ~10-line ID-to-file glob
pattern. Error messages are inconsistent across copies.

## Plan

1. Add `resolveDir(explicit string) (string, error)` — calls findTicketsDir
   when explicit is empty, validates the result is a directory, returns a
   clean error. Replaces boilerplate in check, close, log, migrate, new,
   nextid, ready, archive.

2. Add `resolveTicketByID(dir, id string) (string, error)` — globs for
   NNNN-*.erg, rejects zero or ambiguous matches with consistent messages.
   Replaces boilerplate in close, log, archive.

3. Update each command to call the helpers. No behavior change — identical
   exit codes and error messages (or better: unified wording).

4. Add unit tests for both helpers (missing dir, not-a-dir, ambiguous ID,
   no match, happy path).

## Exit criteria

- `go test ./...` passes.
- `erg check`, `erg validate` produce identical output on the existing
  test corpus.
- Net line count decreases by ≥ 60 lines (conservative; estimate is ~100).
